  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Brief hammering and similar tasks are permitted at a designated station; quieter alternatives remain available during waiting periods.\", \"decision\": \"How should short noisy tasks be coordinated?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers place their names on the noisy-task list, and the steward groups those tasks into announced short periods. People doing quieter work can anticipate interruptions while noisy projects still receive regular access.\nThe studio posts repeating short periods for noisy tasks, and members choose an available turn within those periods. A stable rhythm makes interruptions predictable without requiring a new room-wide negotiation for every task.\nMembers announce a short noisy task at the designated station and wait for nearby members to acknowledge the notice. People close to the sound have time to pause sensitive work before the task begins."
    }
  ],
